What's gotten into him?

241
00:15:21,376 --> 00:15:23,743
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

242
00:15:23,743 --> 00:15:27,543
How badly did you handle the scene
for the news to leak already?

243
00:15:28,576 --> 00:15:32,610
A shooting happened in South Korea.
You really think we can cover it up?

244
00:15:32,610 --> 00:15:34,310
Are you sure it's Kingfisher?

245
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:37,210
It could be someone else.
It could be a copycat crime, for instance.

246
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:38,243
Who would do that?

247
00:15:38,243 --> 00:15:40,543
It's not just any gun.
A sniper shot from 500 meters away?

248
00:15:40,543 --> 00:15:42,543
I mean, besides that guy...

249
00:15:42,543 --> 00:15:45,843
That punk was quiet for four years.

250
00:15:45,843 --> 00:15:49,910
Why now, all of a sudden?
And why our district of all places?

251
00:15:49,910 --> 00:15:51,343
No need for a long explanation.

252
00:15:51,343 --> 00:15:53,476
Can you catch him or not?

253
00:15:53,476 --> 00:15:55,010
We'll investigate.

254
00:15:55,010 --> 00:15:57,043
Good. If you're going to catch him,
do it quickly.

255
00:15:57,043 --> 00:15:59,643
If it looks impossible,
wrap it up quietly when the time is right.

256
00:15:59,643 --> 00:16:02,010
Don't make a big scene for no reason.

257
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:05,343
The higher-ups aren't expecting much anyway.

258
00:16:05,343 --> 00:16:08,810
People considered the best of the best
couldn't catch him for 16 years in 93 tries.

259
00:16:08,810 --> 00:16:11,110
What makes us any different?

260
00:16:12,143 --> 00:16:17,610
Even you, the ace of Violent Crimes,
couldn't catch him once.

261
00:16:22,476 --> 00:16:26,943
If we just drag our feet, he'll probably
move on somewhere else soon.

262
00:16:26,943 --> 00:16:28,576
Just until then...

263
00:16:29,910 --> 00:16:31,576
Hey, I'm talking to you.

264
00:16:31,576 --> 00:16:35,143
Hey, you handle the briefing too.
Just wing it.

265
00:16:41,110 --> 00:16:43,076
[Violent Crimes Team 1]

266
00:16:43,076 --> 00:16:45,143
- You're here.
- Yeah.

267
00:16:50,976 --> 00:16:52,476
What are you doing?

268
00:16:53,876 --> 00:16:57,643
I was curious why he's called Kingfisher,
so I looked it up.

269
00:16:57,643 --> 00:17:00,610
Wow, it just means "kingfisher" in Korean.

270
00:17:00,610 --> 00:17:02,976
I seriously thought it was the kind of bird
that shoots water guns or something.

271
00:17:02,976 --> 00:17:07,543
But apparently, its beak is long
and shaped almost like a sniper rifle.

272
00:17:07,543 --> 00:17:08,935
It perches way up high.

273
00:17:08,935 --> 00:17:12,676
The moment it spots prey,
it shoots into the water like a bullet...

274
00:17:12,676 --> 00:17:14,343
Are you out of your mind?

275
00:17:14,343 --> 00:17:16,810
Is this really the time for you
to be wasting time on this nonsense?

276
00:17:19,910 --> 00:17:24,343
I checked the CCTV center.
Just as we thought, all footage was erased.

277
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:27,310
The witnesses inside the church
were in choir practice at the time,

278
00:17:27,310 --> 00:17:29,543
so they were all gathered in the main hall
and didn't see anything.

279
00:17:29,543 --> 00:17:33,276
The singing was so loud
that they didn't hear anything either.

280
00:17:33,276 --> 00:17:34,643
Choir?

281
00:17:34,643 --> 00:17:37,010
What about the people who drove,
the ones with dashcams?

282
00:17:37,010 --> 00:17:38,976
I already asked about that.

283
00:17:38,976 --> 00:17:41,610
There were seven people
who drove to the church that day.

284
00:17:41,610 --> 00:17:44,135
But the above-ground parking lot
was closed off,

285
00:17:44,135 --> 00:17:46,010
so they all parked underground.

286
00:17:46,010 --> 00:17:51,010
But the church says they never
blocked the above-ground parking lot.

287
00:17:51,010 --> 00:17:55,176
Of course, they didn't.
Someone else must have.

288
00:17:55,176 --> 00:17:56,576
Yeah, someone else...

289
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:59,476
What? What do you mean, someone else?

290
00:18:02,376 --> 00:18:03,876
- Come with me.
- What?

291
00:18:04,576 --> 00:18:08,376
Study all the Kingfisher
case files by tomorrow.

292
00:18:08,376 --> 00:18:10,310
Memorize every single detail.

293
00:18:11,643 --> 00:18:13,543
Got it?

294
00:18:13,543 --> 00:18:15,343
Wait, all this in one day?

295
00:18:15,343 --> 00:18:17,243
This isn't even cramming for an exam.

296
00:18:17,243 --> 00:18:18,343
I'll test you.

297
00:18:18,343 --> 00:18:19,910
Yes, sir!

298
00:18:19,910 --> 00:18:21,510
Good luck.

299
00:18:25,710 --> 00:18:28,376
[The Kingfisher Case Files]

300
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:32,810
When did he even collect all of this?

301
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:33,895
[About Kingfisher,]
<i>Sniper attacks</i>

302
00:18:33,895 --> 00:18:35,943
[are we not catching him,]
<i>are one of the most difficult crimes</i>

303
00:18:35,943 --> 00:18:38,376
[or can we not catch him?]
<i>to investigate and solve.</i>

304
00:18:38,376 --> 00:18:41,319
<i>There are usually no clues
left behind at the crime scene,</i>

305
00:18:41,319 --> 00:18:43,676
<i>such as fingerprints, footprints, or DNA.</i>

306
00:18:43,676 --> 00:18:48,143
<i>It's also extremely difficult to determine
where the shot was fired from.</i>

307
00:18:48,143 --> 00:18:50,176
<i>And even if we take the time to find it,</i>

308
00:18:50,176 --> 00:18:53,310
<i>any traces that may have been
left at the sniper's position</i>

309
00:18:53,310 --> 00:18:54,810
<i>will already be gone.</i>

310
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:57,143
It's been a long time
since I've seen this on the news.

311
00:18:57,143 --> 00:19:00,110
It'll probably be all over the news for days.

312
00:19:00,110 --> 00:19:03,376
By the way, everything's okay, right?

313
00:19:04,276 --> 00:19:07,310
You know what Bo Na's like. Don't worry.

314
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:11,776
Well, I'm not worried or anything,
but... why was her leg shaking?

315
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:14,943
What about you, Team Leader?

316
00:19:14,943 --> 00:19:19,543
Hey, my leg wasn't shaking.
It just cramped up for a second.

317
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:28,176
Fine. Honestly, as the team leader,
I was a little concerned.

318
00:19:28,176 --> 00:19:30,743
It's been four years
since Director Yoo had her baby.

319
00:19:30,743 --> 00:19:35,310
Even athletes worry that they won't be
the same after taking just a year off.

320
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:41,243
I wondered if she might be getting tired
or feeling nervous...

321
00:19:41,243 --> 00:19:44,310
What if she made a mistake?

322
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:46,143
She said it gave her chills.

323
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:49,776
Chills?

324
00:19:49,776 --> 00:19:51,176
It was creepy too.

325
00:19:51,176 --> 00:19:53,143
The great Yoo Bo Na?

326
00:19:57,243 --> 00:20:01,810
Wow, this place really hasn't changed.

327
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:05,010
How do you even breathe, eat, and sleep here?

328
00:20:05,010 --> 00:20:08,343
When was your last health checkup?
Do you ever even go home?

329
00:20:08,343 --> 00:20:12,010
You're here? That was quite a greeting.

330
00:20:12,010 --> 00:20:16,010
Pulled another all-nighter, huh?
What were you tinkering with all night?

331
00:20:16,010 --> 00:20:20,976
The boss wanted me to make something
flow smoothly, like this and that.

332
00:20:20,976 --> 00:20:25,376
So I made it, but I was looking for
one more source.

333
00:20:25,376 --> 00:20:26,810
Oh, really?

334
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:29,510
So I played around with it
like this and that.

335
00:20:29,510 --> 00:20:32,476
And turns out it's a flying fly.
The fly just kind of...

336
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:42,176
You changed your gear a bit?

337
00:20:42,176 --> 00:20:46,676
Oh, you noticed? That's Yoo Bo Na for you.

338
00:20:49,543 --> 00:20:54,310
It's a bit lighter and has less vibration.

339
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:57,176
The ammunition must have changed too.

340
00:20:57,176 --> 00:20:59,510
It's fine. It only took a few months.

341
00:20:59,510 --> 00:21:01,976
- Do you like it?
- Yeah.

342
00:21:01,976 --> 00:21:03,410
Thanks to you, it was much better.

343
00:21:03,410 --> 00:21:07,543
My kid has grown so much lately.
She's 16 kilograms now.

344
00:21:07,543 --> 00:21:09,543
My gift for your comeback.

345
00:21:22,243 --> 00:21:27,176
Yes, Miss! What? What is it?

346
00:21:27,176 --> 00:21:28,710
What?

347
00:21:37,510 --> 00:21:40,976
Wait, you mean what made Director Yoo nervous
was because of her child?

348
00:21:42,410 --> 00:21:45,943
Yul sleeps well, and this morning...

349
00:21:45,943 --> 00:21:50,010
Was Director Yoo in there?
Without even wearing a mask?

350
00:21:50,010 --> 00:21:52,910
Could you let me video call her?
I'll try talking to her.

351
00:21:52,910 --> 00:21:55,076
Yeah, I'll set it up.

352
00:21:57,110 --> 00:21:58,676
Yul!

353
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:03,743
Oh, my Yul! Why don't you want to take a nap?

354
00:22:03,743 --> 00:22:06,043
All your friends are sleeping. Why don't you?

355
00:22:06,043 --> 00:22:09,043
A monster appeared in my dream,
and I'm scared.

356
00:22:09,043 --> 00:22:14,076
Oh, a monster appeared in your dream?
Is that what happened?

357
00:22:14,076 --> 00:22:18,176
Should I sing your favorite Baby Shark's
My Dream Is a Superhero?

358
00:22:18,176 --> 00:22:21,310
You know all the monsters run away
when we sing that song, right?

359
00:22:21,310 --> 00:22:22,543
Alright, good!

360
00:22:22,543 --> 00:22:24,610
<i>Okay, I'm starting! Here we go.</i>

361
00:22:24,610 --> 00:22:27,510
<i>♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪</i>

362
00:22:27,510 --> 00:22:30,210
<i>♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪</i>

363
00:22:30,210 --> 00:22:32,343
<i>♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪</i>

364
00:22:32,343 --> 00:22:35,335
<i>♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪</i>

365
00:22:35,335 --> 00:22:37,135
How is it?

366
00:22:39,110 --> 00:22:42,210
- That gives me chills. It's creepy too.
- You like it?

367
00:22:42,210 --> 00:22:44,943
So, the great Kingfisher has become a mom?

368
00:22:44,943 --> 00:22:48,679
It's unfamiliar. It's very unfamiliar.

369
00:22:48,679 --> 00:22:51,443
<i>♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪</i>

370
00:22:51,443 --> 00:22:54,210
<i>♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪</i>

371
00:22:54,210 --> 00:22:57,043
<i>♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪</i>

372
00:22:57,043 --> 00:23:00,643
<i>♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪</i>

373
00:23:07,976 --> 00:23:11,143
Detective Lee Dong Jin, you're here.

374
00:23:11,143 --> 00:23:14,443
You must be working around the clock
with such a major case

375
00:23:14,443 --> 00:23:16,310
happening in your district.

376
00:23:16,310 --> 00:23:18,510
Please have a seat over here.

377
00:23:18,510 --> 00:23:21,476
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong, it's been a while.

378
00:23:21,476 --> 00:23:24,243
You only come looking for me
when something like this happens.

379
00:23:24,243 --> 00:23:25,943
Sorry.

380
00:23:26,943 --> 00:23:28,676
Hey, you're paying today.

381
00:23:28,676 --> 00:23:31,076
Come on, people are watching. Sit down.

382
00:23:31,076 --> 00:23:33,743
I already ordered. The most expensive one.

383
00:23:38,443 --> 00:23:40,043
Looks expensive.

384
00:23:40,676 --> 00:23:41,910
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yeah.

385
00:23:41,910 --> 00:23:43,576
Thank you.

386
00:23:46,110 --> 00:23:49,943
Just get to the point.
I have to head back right after I eat.

387
00:23:49,943 --> 00:23:53,076
You always act like you're busy.
I'm busy too.

388
00:23:53,943 --> 00:23:57,576
You're covering the Kingfisher story, right?
That's why you're here.

389
00:23:57,576 --> 00:24:01,076
The juniors handle that stuff now.
I've moved on.

390
00:24:01,076 --> 00:24:04,076
You saw the news.
It's exactly what it looks like.

391
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:06,410
Nothing more to tell you.

392
00:24:09,910 --> 00:24:14,910
- No need to get you anything expensive.
- Hey, that's mine. Eat yours.

393
00:24:19,643 --> 00:24:21,443
Is it really the Kingfisher?

394
00:24:23,110 --> 00:24:27,576
Oh, my, why does everyone ask me that
the moment they see me?

395
00:24:28,710 --> 00:24:30,943
If I answer, will you write it?

396
00:24:30,943 --> 00:24:33,410
I told you I wouldn't.

397
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,810
- You won't?
- I won't.

398
00:24:35,810 --> 00:24:37,410
Why not?

399
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:39,543
You're the Kingfisher expert.

400
00:24:39,543 --> 00:24:42,243
Now that I think about it,
four years ago in Haegong-dong too...

401
00:24:42,243 --> 00:24:43,876
Is it Kingfisher?

402
00:24:54,876 --> 00:24:58,543
Well, the method
and victim profiles are similar,

403
00:24:58,543 --> 00:25:00,810
but it's still just speculation.

404
00:25:01,676 --> 00:25:04,076
The weapon is different,

405
00:25:04,076 --> 00:25:07,010
and the fact that he rarely carried out
daytime shootings bothers me.

406
00:25:07,010 --> 00:25:10,710
No, forget the official theory.
What's your gut telling you?

407
00:25:15,310 --> 00:25:18,743
One hundred percent Kingfisher.

408
00:25:22,676 --> 00:25:25,276
I thought he retired four years ago.

409
00:25:25,276 --> 00:25:28,443
Hey, what retirement does a killer have?

410
00:25:30,210 --> 00:25:34,610
What are the differences between
the case four years ago and this one?

411
00:25:34,610 --> 00:25:37,943
You were at both scenes, so you'd know.
Anything, even a small detail.

412
00:25:37,943 --> 00:25:40,510
Like, you found anything
at the shooting site...

413
00:25:41,576 --> 00:25:43,510
You're unbelievable.
Did you come here knowing something?

414
00:25:43,510 --> 00:25:45,743
You found something? What is it?

415
00:25:49,976 --> 00:25:51,476
<i>Baby Shark.</i>

416
00:25:51,476 --> 00:25:53,310
What?

417
00:25:53,310 --> 00:25:54,810
A sticker.

418
00:25:58,510 --> 00:26:00,543
What, a sticker?

419
00:26:00,543 --> 00:26:02,076
Yeah.

420
00:26:03,976 --> 00:26:08,343
I sent it to the NFS just in case,
but they said there were no fingerprints,

421
00:26:08,343 --> 00:26:12,476
and that it was something you could
easily buy at most stores or online.

422
00:26:12,476 --> 00:26:15,910
Which means every household in Korea
with kids probably has one.

423
00:26:15,910 --> 00:26:18,243
Dozens of Baby Sharks.

424
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:22,043
The sharks in our house even have babies.

425
00:26:24,843 --> 00:26:27,643
Looks like Kingfisher
is a Baby Shark fanatic just like my Yul.

426
00:26:27,643 --> 00:26:30,976
Hey, this would blow up the views
if I wrote about it.

427
00:26:38,343 --> 00:26:40,210
This is good.

428
00:26:40,210 --> 00:26:42,776
Yul, what did you play with Chae Won today?

429
00:26:42,776 --> 00:26:45,110
[Baby Shark]
We played with this sticker.

430
00:26:45,110 --> 00:26:46,476
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

431
00:26:46,476 --> 00:26:48,276
Should I stick one on you too? This one?

432
00:26:48,276 --> 00:26:50,143
Should I put one on? Where should I put it?

433
00:26:50,143 --> 00:26:53,610
Mommy is the mommy shark.

434
00:26:53,610 --> 00:26:55,810
Mommy shark?

435
00:26:55,810 --> 00:26:58,676
This makes my clothes look even prettier.

436
00:26:58,676 --> 00:27:01,110
So what did you put on today?

437
00:27:01,110 --> 00:27:03,043
- Baby Shark.
- You put on a Baby Shark?

438
00:27:03,043 --> 00:27:06,043
This one is cute too. It looks like you.

439
00:27:06,043 --> 00:27:07,110
Yul!

440
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:09,276
Daddy!

441
00:27:10,343 --> 00:27:12,476
My little precious!

442
00:27:12,476 --> 00:27:14,610
Come here, my big precious.

443
00:27:18,743 --> 00:27:22,010
Honey, why are you home so early?
Aren't you busy?

444
00:27:22,010 --> 00:27:24,543
I am busy. But today,
in the middle of all that,

445
00:27:24,543 --> 00:27:28,143
I had a sudden realization
that I missed my wife so much!

446
00:27:28,143 --> 00:27:29,910
What could I do then?
I had to run right over.

447
00:27:29,910 --> 00:27:34,443
Really? Why did you miss me so much today?

448
00:27:36,710 --> 00:27:37,910
You did something wrong, right?

449
00:27:37,910 --> 00:27:41,176
What would I have done wrong?
It's not like that, really.

450
00:27:41,176 --> 00:27:44,343
I really just wanted to see you,
so I came. Seriously.

451
00:27:44,343 --> 00:27:48,876
Then we must be connected by telepathy.
I really missed you today too.

452
00:27:48,876 --> 00:27:49,943
Really?

453
00:27:49,943 --> 00:27:51,443
Yeah.

454
00:27:59,543 --> 00:28:03,476
What is it?
Something happened today, didn't it?

455
00:28:03,476 --> 00:28:07,110
What do you mean? I'm just tired
from the business trip yesterday.

456
00:28:07,110 --> 00:28:09,176
Since we're already out,
should we grab dinner before going home?

457
00:28:09,176 --> 00:28:11,110
Yeah! Chicken! Chicken!

458
00:28:11,110 --> 00:28:13,510
Yul, do you want chicken?

459
00:28:13,510 --> 00:28:15,076
Should we go to Grandma's and eat chicken?

460
00:28:15,076 --> 00:28:17,743
Grandma's chicken is the best!

461
00:28:17,743 --> 00:28:19,276
Let's go.

462
00:28:19,276 --> 00:28:22,176
Let's go eat chicken.

463
00:28:29,610 --> 00:28:30,676
Enjoy your meal!

464
00:28:30,676 --> 00:28:32,776
- Let me know if you need anything.
- Grandma, Auntie!

465
00:28:32,776 --> 00:28:34,876
Pretty Yul is here.

466
00:28:34,876 --> 00:28:36,410
What brings you here at this hour?

467
00:28:36,410 --> 00:28:38,535
Oh, my, our pretty Yul is here?

468
00:28:38,535 --> 00:28:40,676
My son is here!

469
00:28:40,676 --> 00:28:42,743
Hey, come out here for a sec.

470
00:28:42,743 --> 00:28:45,243
Why is it so hard to see you these days?

471
00:28:45,243 --> 00:28:48,576
Oh, my, my little Yul!

472
00:28:51,076 --> 00:28:53,743
Yul, say hello to Grandma.
Give her a big greeting.

473
00:28:53,743 --> 00:28:55,576
Hello, Grandma.

474
00:28:55,576 --> 00:28:57,810
Good girl!

475
00:28:57,810 --> 00:29:01,210
But what brings you here?
Did you come straight from work?

476
00:29:01,210 --> 00:29:04,343
We ran into each other near home,
and Yul said she wanted chicken.

477
00:29:04,343 --> 00:29:06,410
Oh, did you?

478
00:29:06,410 --> 00:29:08,743
- Then come sit down. Sit down.
- Sit down.

479
00:29:09,376 --> 00:29:13,110
I will fry up
the most delicious chicken for my Yul!

480
00:29:13,110 --> 00:29:14,643
Okay.

481
00:29:16,176 --> 00:29:18,910
Since you're here anyway, stay and eat.

482
00:29:18,910 --> 00:29:22,476
But it's not good for children or adults
to eat takeout food too often.

483
00:29:22,476 --> 00:29:26,743
People who work outside all day
should come home to a warm homemade meal.

484
00:29:26,743 --> 00:29:28,743
It was me who wanted it.

485
00:29:28,743 --> 00:29:30,876
Okay, Mother.

486
00:29:32,776 --> 00:29:34,276
I was the one who asked...

487
00:29:35,410 --> 00:29:36,443
Welcome!

488
00:29:36,443 --> 00:29:39,743
- Sun Il, I should've done that. Sorry.
- Oh, please, sit down.

489
00:29:39,743 --> 00:29:42,143
Hey, hold it in today.

490
00:29:42,143 --> 00:29:44,643
Mom's finally in a good mood
after a while. Don't ruin it.

491
00:29:44,643 --> 00:29:48,076
Why? Why is Mom in a good mood?

492
00:29:48,076 --> 00:29:51,476
The landlord said
they'd freeze the rent again.

493
00:29:51,476 --> 00:29:55,810
Other shops raise their rent every year,
but ours hasn't changed for years.

494
00:29:55,810 --> 00:29:58,576
She was bragging about it to everyone.

495
00:29:58,576 --> 00:30:01,610
That's really kind of the landlord.
It's not easy to do that these days.

496
00:30:01,610 --> 00:30:03,643
Such an angel.

497
00:30:03,643 --> 00:30:05,643
We're busy right now, so wait just a little.

498
00:30:05,643 --> 00:30:07,110
Wait just a moment, Yul.

499
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:08,643
Okay.

500
00:30:09,543 --> 00:30:12,210
I'm back!

501
00:30:12,210 --> 00:30:14,076
Bo Na, you're here?

502
00:30:14,076 --> 00:30:15,143
Auntie!

503
00:30:15,143 --> 00:30:18,576
Oh, my! Our cute Yul is here?

504
00:30:18,576 --> 00:30:20,443
Did you just finish a delivery?

505
00:30:20,443 --> 00:30:22,503
Yeah. Is it some special day?

506
00:30:22,503 --> 00:30:25,343
We got a bunch of
delivery orders all at once.

507
00:30:25,343 --> 00:30:26,676
You said you'd drink water, so drink up.

508
00:30:26,676 --> 00:30:29,810
By the way, why are you here
at this hour? Aren't you busy?

509
00:30:29,810 --> 00:30:31,210
I heard Kingfisher showed up.

510
00:30:31,210 --> 00:30:33,127
That was ages ago.
That's not my thing anymore.

511
00:30:33,127 --> 00:30:35,676
What about you? So, how have you been?

512
00:30:35,676 --> 00:30:37,910
Seriously, what have you been
hearing all this time?

513
00:30:37,910 --> 00:30:39,576
Same old, same old.

514
00:30:39,576 --> 00:30:43,543
I mean, I do have a social position
as a graduate student.

515
00:30:43,543 --> 00:30:47,110
But to Mom, that's the same
as being an unemployed bum.

516
00:30:47,110 --> 00:30:48,543
- Ah, seriously...
- That's why

517
00:30:48,543 --> 00:30:50,310
I keep telling you to hire part-timers.

518
00:30:50,310 --> 00:30:53,095
How can we afford
to hire people and pay them?

519
00:30:53,095 --> 00:30:54,876
Family members have to work hard together.

520
00:30:54,876 --> 00:30:59,476
You exploit your daughter for cheap labor.
You're a terrible employer!

521
00:30:59,476 --> 00:31:01,276
A terrible employer.

522
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:03,076
All you do is talk.

523
00:31:03,076 --> 00:31:04,610
You know your sister-in-law
went back to work, right?

524
00:31:04,610 --> 00:31:07,376
- Yeah.
- If you look after Yul sometimes,

525
00:31:07,376 --> 00:31:12,543
I might, you know, increase your allowance.

526
00:31:12,543 --> 00:31:14,010
Really?

527
00:31:14,010 --> 00:31:18,876
Of course, I'd do anything for our Yul
even without allowance!

528
00:31:18,876 --> 00:31:22,343
But if you offer, I'll gladly accept.

529
00:31:23,243 --> 00:31:26,610
- I'll chip in too. Please help us.
- Done!

530
00:31:26,610 --> 00:31:29,043
Bo Na, how is it being back
at work? Do you like it?

531
00:31:29,043 --> 00:31:31,710
Oh, there's no way it could be good.
Is the work manageable?

532
00:31:31,710 --> 00:31:32,976
[Tae Seong Chicken]
Oh, dear.

533
00:31:32,976 --> 00:31:35,110
Why are you sitting in the customer's seat?
Hurry and go deliver.

534
00:31:35,110 --> 00:31:37,143
How is he a customer?

535
00:31:37,143 --> 00:31:38,676
The deliveries are piling up.

536
00:31:38,676 --> 00:31:40,276
Then at least pay me more.

537
00:31:40,276 --> 00:31:41,810
I'll be back.

538
00:31:46,076 --> 00:31:49,043
Did he go to prison for another crime?

539
00:31:49,043 --> 00:31:51,543
Was he seriously injured or sick?

540
00:31:52,263 --> 00:31:55,976
A vacation... A leave of absence?

541
00:31:55,976 --> 00:31:57,576
You've been saying that since earlier.

542
00:31:57,576 --> 00:32:01,843
What? Is being a murderer a job?
Retirement, leave of absence, vacation?

543
00:32:06,010 --> 00:32:10,876
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

544
00:32:10,876 --> 00:32:13,376
Even Kingfisher
could get married, unlike you...

545
00:32:14,076 --> 00:32:16,076
Watch what you say.
There's a gun at the station.

546
00:32:16,076 --> 00:32:17,710
Hey, that's disgusting! Hey!

547
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:19,527
That's why you should get married, idiot.

548
00:32:19,527 --> 00:32:22,010
Stop living alone like some pathetic loser.

549
00:32:23,623 --> 00:32:27,643
Fine, let's say
your ridiculous theory is true.

550
00:32:27,643 --> 00:32:31,111
If he got married, built a family,
and had a kid, why come back?

551
00:32:31,111 --> 00:32:32,810
Why not just keep living that life?

552
00:32:32,810 --> 00:32:34,243
Because he couldn't stand not killing people?

553
00:32:34,243 --> 00:32:37,443
Or what, because he's some hero
who wants attention?

554
00:32:37,443 --> 00:32:40,676
Or maybe because life got boring?

555
00:32:41,476 --> 00:32:44,676
Why are you asking me?
Ask him yourself when you catch him.

556
00:32:44,676 --> 00:32:47,879
And ask him if he's really
a Baby Shark fanatic too.

557
00:32:47,879 --> 00:32:49,447
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

558
00:32:49,447 --> 00:32:52,843
That sticker might really have been a clue.

559
00:32:52,843 --> 00:32:55,043
<i>You never know.</i>

560
00:33:08,676 --> 00:33:09,910
Daddy, it's good.

561
00:33:09,910 --> 00:33:11,510
Is it good?

562
00:33:11,510 --> 00:33:13,576
I think it's delicious too.

563
00:33:15,710 --> 00:33:20,443
Yul, you can do this, right?

564
00:33:23,015 --> 00:33:24,576
I'll give it to you.

565
00:33:27,527 --> 00:33:28,943
Is it good?

566
00:33:28,943 --> 00:33:30,843
Yul, you learned how to do this, right?

567
00:33:30,843 --> 00:33:33,443
You're a big girl now,
so you can do it, right?

568
00:33:47,643 --> 00:33:49,735
[Yoo Bo Na's Relationship Chart]

569
00:33:59,743 --> 00:34:02,247
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3,
Killer Group]

570
00:35:32,776 --> 00:35:36,076
You're already awake? It's still early.

571
00:35:36,076 --> 00:35:37,810
I had a bad dream.

572
00:35:37,810 --> 00:35:42,710
I woke up and got scared
because you weren't there.

573
00:35:42,710 --> 00:35:44,943
A bad dream? What kind of dream?

574
00:35:44,943 --> 00:35:46,743
A dream where someone took you away.

575
00:35:46,743 --> 00:35:50,043
Who? Who took me?

576
00:35:50,043 --> 00:35:51,110
A monster.

577
00:35:51,110 --> 00:35:52,576
What? What is that?

578
00:35:52,576 --> 00:35:56,076
It's real. In my dream,
a really scary monster took you away.

579
00:35:56,076 --> 00:35:58,210
You're in big trouble now.

580
00:35:59,776 --> 00:36:04,710
No, maybe I'm the one who's in trouble.
I can't live without you.

581
00:36:04,710 --> 00:36:07,943
Then I guess I should sing
Baby Shark's Superhero for you.

582
00:36:07,943 --> 00:36:09,776
Apparently, it's the perfect weapon
against monsters.

583
00:36:09,776 --> 00:36:11,410
- Really?
- Yeah.

584
00:36:11,410 --> 00:36:12,810
Sing it.

585
00:36:12,810 --> 00:36:13,843
Sing it for me.

586
00:36:13,843 --> 00:36:18,210
Go back inside and get some more sleep.
I'll take Yul to daycare today.

587
00:36:26,110 --> 00:36:29,510
Let's just stay like this for one minute.

588
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:44,543
[Durumi Electronics]

589
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:10,610
Good morning!

590
00:38:29,510 --> 00:38:31,276
[Security Alert]

591
00:38:34,243 --> 00:38:37,976
Hey, when did Tae Min leave
without saying anything?

592
00:38:39,610 --> 00:38:42,110
[Unregistered Entrant Detected]
What, he brought someone with him?

593
00:38:44,176 --> 00:38:47,776
She's finally here! Our team's newbie!

594
00:38:48,710 --> 00:38:50,610
Wow!

595
00:38:52,343 --> 00:38:53,943
[Bong Tae Min]

596
00:38:57,535 --> 00:38:58,535
[Not Today]

597
00:38:58,535 --> 00:39:00,610
What? The case has been...

598
00:39:02,510 --> 00:39:04,476
The case has been closed?

599
00:39:06,576 --> 00:39:08,076
Just a moment.

600
00:39:09,776 --> 00:39:11,310
The investigation is already over?

601
00:39:11,310 --> 00:39:13,043
What about the NFS results?
Did they come out?

602
00:39:13,043 --> 00:39:16,410
They did come out,
but there was nothing significant.

603
00:39:16,410 --> 00:39:17,443
[Bae Doo Hyuk Car Explosion Case]

604
00:39:17,443 --> 00:39:21,210
It has been classified
as an accidental death.

605
00:39:21,210 --> 00:39:22,810
An accidental death?

606
00:39:22,810 --> 00:39:25,110
So you're saying it wasn't murder,
but an accident?

607
00:39:25,110 --> 00:39:29,710
Wow, our new employee
brought this on her first day.

608
00:39:29,710 --> 00:39:31,710
She's got great taste, right?

609
00:39:31,710 --> 00:39:32,810
Yeah.

610
00:39:32,810 --> 00:39:35,843
Then we should do proper introductions.

611
00:39:35,843 --> 00:39:38,310
As I've mentioned before,

612
00:39:38,310 --> 00:39:42,210
this is our new team member
who will be working with us, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

613
00:39:43,576 --> 00:39:46,710
Nice to meet you.
I look forward to working with you.

614
00:39:46,710 --> 00:39:48,343
Welcome!

615
00:39:51,276 --> 00:39:53,143
Same here. It's nice to meet you.

616
00:39:53,143 --> 00:39:57,127
Oh, Ms. Hyun Nam has been working alone
as a freelancer until now,

617
00:39:57,127 --> 00:39:59,591
so this is her first time working
in a team and company environment.

618
00:39:59,591 --> 00:40:01,643
Please help her out.

619
00:40:01,643 --> 00:40:04,176
Let me properly introduce everyone
on our team.

620
00:40:04,176 --> 00:40:07,043
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol.

621
00:40:07,043 --> 00:40:10,710
Her job is forging all kinds of documents.

622
00:40:10,710 --> 00:40:12,943
- How well?
- Perfectly.

623
00:40:12,943 --> 00:40:14,407
[Business Trip Application]
<i>Please come to me</i>

624
00:40:14,407 --> 00:40:15,576
<i>for anything related to paperwork.</i>

625
00:40:15,576 --> 00:40:18,910
[Destination: Musan, Reason: Client Meeting]

626
00:40:19,976 --> 00:40:21,543
Alright.

627
00:40:21,543 --> 00:40:22,876
You startled me.

628
00:40:22,876 --> 00:40:27,576
Were you there the whole time?
That's Manager Bong Tae Min.

629
00:40:27,576 --> 00:40:29,031
We don't call him Manager Bong, though.

630
00:40:29,031 --> 00:40:31,710
We call him Manager Tae or Manager Tae Min.

631
00:40:31,710 --> 00:40:35,676
He handles the cutting-edge equipment there.

632
00:40:37,110 --> 00:40:39,510
Well, that guy...

633
00:40:39,510 --> 00:40:41,510
Is he kept isolated separately?

634
00:40:41,510 --> 00:40:44,676
Isolated? Well, yeah.
It's more of self-isolation.

635
00:40:44,676 --> 00:40:47,710
None of us likes going into that room.

636
00:40:47,710 --> 00:40:49,543
You'll understand later.

637
00:40:53,110 --> 00:40:57,376
It's simple. No need for a long explanation.

638
00:40:57,376 --> 00:40:59,776
<i>A portable LPG gas canister,
burned completely black,</i>

639
00:40:59,776 --> 00:41:02,919
was found in the trunk of Bae Doo Hyuk's car.

640
00:41:02,919 --> 00:41:06,279
It turns out the valve was slightly open.

641
00:41:06,279 --> 00:41:08,076
This is...

642
00:41:08,076 --> 00:41:11,610
better known as Dr. Go.

643
00:41:11,610 --> 00:41:16,610
His job is making any death
look like a medical accident.

644
00:41:16,610 --> 00:41:17,710
How well?

645
00:41:17,710 --> 00:41:19,676
Perfectly.

646
00:41:19,676 --> 00:41:21,710
<i>I'm a real doctor.</i>

647
00:41:29,110 --> 00:41:31,543
The driver is going to the restroom.

648
00:41:31,543 --> 00:41:32,576
<i>Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.</i>

649
00:41:32,576 --> 00:41:36,610
Oh, he can do anything with computers.
He's our team's genius hacker.

650
00:41:37,543 --> 00:41:39,476
Nice to meet you.

651
00:41:39,476 --> 00:41:40,976
Yeah.

652
00:41:42,210 --> 00:41:45,710
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

653
00:41:45,710 --> 00:41:49,351
I'm Kim Bong Pal,

654
00:41:49,351 --> 00:41:53,176
the leader of Sales Team 3.

655
00:41:53,176 --> 00:41:57,710
My last name is actually Kim,
but everyone just calls me Team Leader Bong.

656
00:42:00,876 --> 00:42:02,576
What I do is...

657
00:42:07,843 --> 00:42:10,510
<i>You're saying there are
absolutely no signs of foul play?</i>

658
00:42:10,510 --> 00:42:14,210
<i>If someone put the gas tank in there
or deliberately opened the valve...</i>

659
00:42:14,210 --> 00:42:17,376
<i>Then there should've been footage of it.</i>

660
00:42:17,376 --> 00:42:20,243
<i>But we checked all the CCTV outside the club</i>

661
00:42:20,243 --> 00:42:23,010
<i>and all the dashcam footage
from the parking lot, and there's nothing.</i>

662
00:42:23,010 --> 00:42:25,676
<i>It was pure luck. A miracle.</i>

663
00:42:25,676 --> 00:42:29,143
<i>Well, there's usually a separate driver.</i>

664
00:42:29,143 --> 00:42:31,676
<i>But that day the driver
had a sudden stomach problem.</i>

665
00:42:31,676 --> 00:42:35,176
<i>Well, as for the gas tank,
Bae Doo Hyuk must've put it there himself.</i>

666
00:42:35,176 --> 00:42:37,443
<i>You know where Bae Doo Hyuk was going?</i>

667
00:42:37,443 --> 00:42:39,810
<i>His girlfriend was waiting
for him at a nearby villa.</i>

668
00:42:39,810 --> 00:42:42,810
<i>Maybe they were planning to have
a barbecue together or something.</i>

669
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:45,576
<i>At least it happened
in a quiet suburban area.</i>

670
00:42:45,576 --> 00:42:47,610
<i>If it had happened downtown...</i>

671
00:42:47,610 --> 00:42:49,443
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

672
00:42:49,443 --> 00:42:52,243
Quiet location. Good.

673
00:42:52,243 --> 00:42:56,910
Once the taxi is more than
100 meters away, we'll go.

674
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:02,043
Now, client meeting starts.

675
00:43:13,976 --> 00:43:15,776
Meeting clear.

676
00:43:17,310 --> 00:43:21,343
Rest in peace. I can't tell you to be reborn.

677
00:43:21,343 --> 00:43:25,210
Whether they die or survive,
I make it all look like an accident.

678
00:43:25,210 --> 00:43:27,243
How well? Perfectly.

679
00:43:27,243 --> 00:43:32,143
Simply put, you could say
he died an unfortunate death.

680
00:43:32,143 --> 00:43:33,976
<i>What a fate...</i>

681
00:43:34,643 --> 00:43:36,610
Isn't something a little strange?

682
00:43:36,610 --> 00:43:40,276
Everything lines up perfectly.
Like someone planned the whole thing.

683
00:43:40,276 --> 00:43:42,976
Bae Doo Hyuk wasn't just involved in drugs.

684
00:43:42,976 --> 00:43:47,343
He was known for framing his underlings
for murders he ordered.

685
00:43:47,343 --> 00:43:49,010
<i>It's a known fact in that world.</i>

686
00:43:49,010 --> 00:43:52,476
Who knows how many
other crimes he got away with?

687
00:43:52,476 --> 00:43:54,443
Exactly my point.
Which is why it is even more...

688
00:43:54,443 --> 00:43:55,610
<i>He was such a piece of work.</i>

689
00:43:55,610 --> 00:43:59,776
Honestly, a guy like him getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

690
00:43:59,776 --> 00:44:01,943
Well, detectives speak with evidence,

691
00:44:01,943 --> 00:44:04,210
and you, the reporter,
should write with facts.

692
00:44:04,210 --> 00:44:07,910
<i>With everyone already worked up
over Kingfisher, who would even care?</i>

693
00:44:07,910 --> 00:44:11,376
Anyway, we've closed the case,
so just know that.

694
00:44:11,376 --> 00:44:13,671
And don't call me again.

695
00:44:13,671 --> 00:44:14,876
Hello...

696
00:44:14,876 --> 00:44:17,443
<i>But public sentiment is different.</i>

697
00:44:17,443 --> 00:44:20,710
<i>Because he only targets the worst criminals,</i>

698
00:44:20,710 --> 00:44:24,376
<i>some people are becoming
obsessed with Kingfisher.</i>

699
00:44:24,376 --> 00:44:27,176
<i>The Kingfisher fan club
already has over a million members.</i>

700
00:44:27,176 --> 00:44:28,610
<i>He targets the worst of the worst,</i>

701
00:44:28,610 --> 00:44:32,376
<i>especially those
who escaped proper punishment,</i>

702
00:44:32,376 --> 00:44:35,110
<i>so isn't it natural that people frustrated
with the flawed justice system</i>

703
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:36,910
<i>are drawn to him?</i>

704
00:44:36,910 --> 00:44:41,310
<i>A powerful hero who punishes evil
in place of a powerless law.</i>

705
00:44:41,310 --> 00:44:44,376
Lastly, our ace.

706
00:44:44,376 --> 00:44:48,576
The face of Sales Team 3, Director Yoo Bo Na.

707
00:44:50,610 --> 00:44:52,043
As for Director Yoo...

708
00:44:52,043 --> 00:44:54,776
I know who she is.

709
00:45:05,143 --> 00:45:08,810
It's an honor to meet you, Kingfisher.

710
00:45:15,343 --> 00:45:18,976
The pleasure's mine, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

711
00:45:21,743 --> 00:45:25,243
Let's work well together from now on.

712
00:45:25,243 --> 00:45:26,743
"Together"?

713
00:45:30,710 --> 00:45:32,843
Yeah, let's work well together.

714
00:45:40,043 --> 00:45:41,143
Where's my desk?

715
00:45:41,143 --> 00:45:44,310
Oh, right here. Next to Assistant Manager Ki.

716
00:45:45,376 --> 00:45:48,776
All right, everyone. Back to work.

717
00:45:51,110 --> 00:45:52,810
Oh, right.

718
00:45:52,810 --> 00:45:55,043
I forgot to tell you what I do.

719
00:45:55,043 --> 00:45:56,643
Oh, you're right.

720
00:45:57,376 --> 00:45:59,043
I handle poisonings.

721
00:45:59,043 --> 00:46:02,631
Slip poison into food or drinks,
and no one ever knows perfectly.

722
00:46:06,476 --> 00:46:10,210
So, how about pork belly with water dropwort
for tonight's team dinner?

723
00:46:10,210 --> 00:46:11,310
Water dropwort is great for detoxing.

724
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,510
Then make the arrangements.

725
00:46:12,510 --> 00:46:15,543
- Yeah, I'll book the place.
- Good.

726
00:46:27,943 --> 00:46:31,276
I've finished the article, so it's fine.

727
00:46:31,276 --> 00:46:36,476
I'll take care of Yul,
so don't worry and enjoy yourself.

728
00:46:36,476 --> 00:46:42,243
It's your welcome-back dinner too.
The guest of honor can't miss it.

729
00:46:42,243 --> 00:46:44,510
Then I'm counting on you tonight.

730
00:46:44,510 --> 00:46:47,210
When you get home,
wash Yul's hands and feet first, okay?

731
00:46:47,210 --> 00:46:50,510
And there's curry
and beef radish soup in the fridge...

732
00:46:50,510 --> 00:46:53,043
I can handle it.

733
00:46:54,243 --> 00:46:58,676
Okay, lecture over! I'll call you
when we're wrapping up.

734
00:46:58,676 --> 00:47:00,176
See you later.

735
00:47:06,023 --> 00:47:08,423
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

736
00:47:17,511 --> 00:47:18,511
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

737
00:47:21,310 --> 00:47:22,943
That's over, I see.

738
00:47:25,810 --> 00:47:27,143
Yeah, well, for now.

739
00:47:27,143 --> 00:47:30,210
"For now"? Does that mean
there's a second step?

740
00:47:30,210 --> 00:47:33,143
Forget it. From now on,
you're going after Kingfisher, right?

741
00:47:33,143 --> 00:47:35,210
"What did he do for 4 years,
and why did he come back without dying?"

742
00:47:35,210 --> 00:47:36,276
Well, something more in-depth.

743
00:47:36,276 --> 00:47:37,376
I'll get going.

744
00:47:37,376 --> 00:47:39,510
Oh, leaving already?

745
00:47:39,510 --> 00:47:42,610
Where to first? The NFS?
The crime scene? The police station?

746
00:47:42,610 --> 00:47:44,610
No. I'm picking up my daughter.

747
00:47:44,610 --> 00:47:46,776
- Your daughter?
- My wife is running late today.

748
00:47:46,776 --> 00:47:48,310
Oh, boy.

749
00:47:48,310 --> 00:47:50,110
I'll get going then.

750
00:47:50,110 --> 00:47:52,676
Hey, Tae Seong, you punk!

751
00:47:53,776 --> 00:47:55,303
Well, what's gotten into him?

752
00:47:55,303 --> 00:47:57,927
One bottle of soju, please!

753
00:47:59,410 --> 00:48:00,576
Dig in, everyone.

754
00:48:00,576 --> 00:48:02,376
Yeah.

755
00:48:02,376 --> 00:48:07,610
Director Yoo, don't you ever
get to eat meat at home or...

756
00:48:09,543 --> 00:48:14,810
We're more of a chicken family.
This pork is really amazing.

757
00:48:14,810 --> 00:48:18,243
The best part about coming back to work
is definitely the company dinners.

758
00:48:18,243 --> 00:48:21,823
Absolutely. Team dinners
are the best part of office life.

759
00:48:21,823 --> 00:48:22,823
That's true.

760
00:48:22,823 --> 00:48:24,343
- Alright.
- Cheers!

761
00:48:24,343 --> 00:48:26,376
Sales Team 3, fighting!

762
00:48:26,376 --> 00:48:29,351
- Fighting!
- Cheers!

763
00:48:34,643 --> 00:48:36,176
This is so good.

764
00:48:36,176 --> 00:48:37,210
Good, huh?

765
00:48:37,210 --> 00:48:39,010
Want a drink, Ms. Yoo?

766
00:48:41,410 --> 00:48:43,376
Oh, no!

767
00:48:43,376 --> 00:48:45,943
- Don't.
- I'll just smell it.

768
00:48:47,976 --> 00:48:50,876
Director Yoo hasn't touched alcohol
since she got married.

769
00:48:50,876 --> 00:48:57,043
Honestly, that's for the best.
She gets pretty wild when she drinks.

770
00:48:58,610 --> 00:49:01,476
By the way, I was really surprised.

771
00:49:01,476 --> 00:49:04,243
I heard that Hyun Nam
is the developer of that famous 'Mist'?

772
00:49:04,243 --> 00:49:06,243
Exactly.

773
00:49:06,243 --> 00:49:09,343
Now that Director Yoo is back

774
00:49:09,343 --> 00:49:10,810
and someone as talented
as Hyun Nam has joined us,

775
00:49:10,810 --> 00:49:15,276
Sales Team 3 is basically
the Avengers now, right?

776
00:49:15,276 --> 00:49:16,610
Absolutely.

777
00:49:16,610 --> 00:49:19,376
By the way, what exactly is 'Mist'?

778
00:49:19,376 --> 00:49:22,743
I guess you don't know about it,
Assistant Manager Yang.

779
00:49:26,176 --> 00:49:28,143
Gather around.

780
00:49:30,151 --> 00:49:37,010
Mist is the name of the poison
that's claimed the most lives

781
00:49:37,010 --> 00:49:39,076
in recent years.

782
00:49:39,076 --> 00:49:41,476
It's about 10,000 times
more toxic than arsenic

783
00:49:41,476 --> 00:49:44,910
and roughly 100 times
more potent than tetrodotoxin.

784
00:49:44,910 --> 00:49:49,876
No autopsy will ever detect a trace of it.

785
00:49:49,876 --> 00:49:54,876
By then, it naturally breaks down
and leaves almost no trace in the body.

786
00:49:54,876 --> 00:49:57,910
What do you think? Perfectly, right?

787
00:49:59,243 --> 00:50:03,776
For our line of work,
it's the perfect poison.

788
00:50:04,576 --> 00:50:06,743
That's incredible!

789
00:50:06,743 --> 00:50:09,376
How did you create something like that?

790
00:50:09,376 --> 00:50:11,776
Well, it just happened.

791
00:50:11,776 --> 00:50:13,643
"Well, it just happened."

792
00:50:15,176 --> 00:50:16,543
But I'm curious.

793
00:50:16,543 --> 00:50:19,476
With skills like yours,
you could've stayed independent.

794
00:50:20,143 --> 00:50:23,010
Why join this team?

795
00:50:25,143 --> 00:50:26,143
Hold on.

796
00:50:26,143 --> 00:50:27,676
Oh, Director Yoo!

797
00:50:30,276 --> 00:50:32,710
I have a debt to repay.

798
00:50:36,510 --> 00:50:37,543
What did you do today, Yul?

799
00:50:37,543 --> 00:50:39,343
<i>Ta-da!</i>

800
00:50:39,343 --> 00:50:41,376
<i>I drew Mommy and Daddy, and Yul.</i>

801
00:50:41,376 --> 00:50:43,610
Wow, that's a great drawing, Yul!

802
00:50:43,610 --> 00:50:45,976
But why did you draw Daddy better?

803
00:50:45,976 --> 00:50:51,576
<i>Because Yul loves Daddy more, right?</i>

804
00:50:51,576 --> 00:50:55,719
No, Yul loves Mommy more, right?
You love Mommy more, don't you?

805
00:50:55,719 --> 00:51:01,735
<i>No. I love both Mommy and Daddy.</i>

806
00:51:02,710 --> 00:51:07,743
I love Yul too. Love you! Heart!

807
00:51:07,743 --> 00:51:09,210
I'll be home soon.

808
00:51:09,210 --> 00:51:12,143
<i>See you later, Mommy!</i>

809
00:51:13,443 --> 00:51:14,643
So cute.

810
00:51:14,643 --> 00:51:17,310
It's a shame no one else
gets to see it, Kingfisher.

811
00:51:17,310 --> 00:51:19,943
You're having all the fun by yourself.

812
00:51:28,476 --> 00:51:31,543
Don't worry. No one would believe it anyway.

813
00:51:31,543 --> 00:51:36,310
Who'd ever imagine
the infamous Kingfisher is a married mom?

814
00:51:49,910 --> 00:51:53,076
Hyun Nam, do you have Mist?

815
00:51:55,143 --> 00:52:01,176
No, not the drinkable kind, the spray kind.
My clothes smell like pork barbecue.

816
00:52:01,176 --> 00:52:02,727
Got any?

817
00:52:02,727 --> 00:52:04,327
Oh, gosh.

818
00:52:11,210 --> 00:52:13,810
A lot of people would be disappointed.

819
00:52:13,810 --> 00:52:15,943
You're practically worshiped as a hero.

820
00:52:15,943 --> 00:52:18,876
If they found out you're living
such an ordinary family life...

821
00:52:18,876 --> 00:52:20,776
You think so?

822
00:52:20,776 --> 00:52:25,443
Have you ever wished you could
go back to your old life?

823
00:52:27,476 --> 00:52:30,210
Even married women say
they think that sometimes.

824
00:52:30,210 --> 00:52:35,143
Like wanting to go back to the carefree,
glamorous days of being single.

825
00:52:35,776 --> 00:52:39,643
Not at all. I like my life now.

826
00:52:40,876 --> 00:52:44,476
Because everything
that matters to me is right here.

827
00:52:45,576 --> 00:52:47,776
I see.

828
00:52:47,776 --> 00:52:49,343
Then why did you come back?

829
00:52:49,343 --> 00:52:51,843
You could've just kept living
that happy little life.

830
00:52:51,843 --> 00:52:54,276
Then why did you join this team, Hyun Nam?

831
00:52:54,276 --> 00:52:56,710
Did you come here to see me?

832
00:52:56,710 --> 00:53:00,410
Well, it just seemed like
you've been watching me all night.

833
00:53:00,410 --> 00:53:04,676
I wondered if you were my fan.
Or maybe an anti-fan?

834
00:53:04,676 --> 00:53:08,876
They say former fans
make the scariest haters.

835
00:53:08,876 --> 00:53:12,143
That's a little childish.

836
00:53:18,210 --> 00:53:22,676
Oh Hyun Nam, everyone makes choices.

837
00:53:22,676 --> 00:53:26,110
Those choices shape a person's life.

838
00:53:26,110 --> 00:53:28,967
Everyone makes
what they believe is the best choice

839
00:53:28,967 --> 00:53:31,276
because their life matters to them.

840
00:53:31,276 --> 00:53:35,143
And I think those choices deserve respect.

841
00:53:35,143 --> 00:53:36,910
I'm not here to listen to lectures...

842
00:53:36,910 --> 00:53:43,076
Just like it was your own choice
to do this work and join this company.

843
00:53:43,076 --> 00:53:47,343
No one forced you in
or pushed you out, right?

844
00:53:52,443 --> 00:53:56,676
If you're looking to play hero,
you've come to the wrong place.

845
00:53:56,676 --> 00:53:59,776
That's for Baby Sharks.

846
00:53:59,776 --> 00:54:01,510
Not us.

847
00:54:03,610 --> 00:54:05,376
What if...

848
00:54:06,343 --> 00:54:10,310
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

849
00:54:12,410 --> 00:54:13,910
I don't know.

850
00:54:14,843 --> 00:54:16,876
I've never thought about it.

851
00:54:17,543 --> 00:54:19,476
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

852
00:54:35,476 --> 00:54:38,010
[Caller ID Restricted:
I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

853
00:55:05,210 --> 00:55:06,543
May I take your order?

854
00:55:06,543 --> 00:55:09,510
One iced Americano, please.

855
00:55:14,610 --> 00:55:18,010
<i>Are you going to be late today?
I'm finishing early today.</i>

856
00:55:18,876 --> 00:55:20,343
<i>Really?</i>

857
00:55:20,343 --> 00:55:23,276
<i>I just have one meeting with an informant,
and then I'll be done too.</i>

858
00:55:24,310 --> 00:55:26,943
<i>Then how about we go on a date for a change?</i>

859
00:55:26,943 --> 00:55:30,376
<i>Se Ah said she'll watch Yul.
Guess she could use a little spending money.</i>

860
00:55:32,243 --> 00:55:36,376
<i>Of course, it's okay with me.
As expected, the power of pocket money!</i>

861
00:55:40,110 --> 00:55:41,710
Thanks!

862
00:55:58,743 --> 00:55:59,976
Alright!

863
00:55:59,976 --> 00:56:04,810
Today is your last chance to take it easy,
so head home early.

864
00:56:04,810 --> 00:56:09,076
And you all know vacation days
are off the table for a while, right?

865
00:56:09,076 --> 00:56:12,543
So get some rest while you can.

866
00:56:12,543 --> 00:56:14,476
Good work. Get home safely.

867
00:56:14,476 --> 00:56:16,010
Yes, sir.

868
00:56:18,443 --> 00:56:20,710
But Oh Hyun Nam is something else.

869
00:56:20,710 --> 00:56:23,843
Taking a personal day
on her second day of work.

870
00:56:25,010 --> 00:56:27,243
She must've had something urgent.

871
00:56:27,243 --> 00:56:31,943
Let's let it slide this time.

872
00:56:33,043 --> 00:56:34,776
Yeah.

873
00:56:34,776 --> 00:56:36,310
Go home, everyone.

874
00:56:58,010 --> 00:56:59,367
[Honey, I've arrived. When will you get here?
Where are you, Tae Seong?]

875
00:57:02,276 --> 00:57:03,591
[New Message]

876
00:57:15,559 --> 00:57:18,943
Well, Assistant Manager Ki,
why are you still here?

877
00:57:20,943 --> 00:57:24,576
What have you been working on all day?

878
00:57:24,576 --> 00:57:29,076
I figured out
why Oh Hyun Nam joined our team.

879
00:57:30,343 --> 00:57:32,076
What are you talking about?

880
00:57:32,943 --> 00:57:34,110
Oh, Director Yoo!

881
00:57:34,110 --> 00:57:35,376
Ms. Yoo, you came just in time.

882
00:57:35,376 --> 00:57:36,943
- Oh Hyun Nam...
- Please track where this message came from.

883
00:57:36,943 --> 00:57:38,543
As fast as you can.

884
00:57:42,076 --> 00:57:47,276
What is this? What's going on?
What about Oh Hyun Nam?

885
00:57:47,276 --> 00:57:51,043
<i>See if you can find me. But come alone.</i>

886
00:57:51,043 --> 00:57:53,243
<i>If you're not here before eight,
whatever happens is on you.</i>

887
00:57:53,243 --> 00:57:54,810
It's for Bo Na.

888
00:57:56,376 --> 00:57:58,543
She came to meet her.

889
00:58:05,276 --> 00:58:07,043
What do you mean?

890
00:58:27,276 --> 00:58:30,776
[Archived Portraits]
Oh Hyun Nam. Real name, Oh Seung Ah.

891
00:58:30,776 --> 00:58:32,476
<i>Fifteen years ago, in winter,</i>

892
00:58:32,476 --> 00:58:35,876
<i>Oh Seung Ah's dad, Oh Man Seok,
was released from prison.</i>

893
00:58:35,876 --> 00:58:38,676
<i>He went straight to see his daughter.</i>

894
00:58:38,676 --> 00:58:40,910
<i>That Christmas night,</i>

895
00:58:42,310 --> 00:58:45,176
<i>Bo Na killed Oh Seung Ah's dad.</i>

896
00:58:45,976 --> 00:58:48,243
<i>Right in front of her.</i>

897
00:58:50,243 --> 00:58:51,776
So...

898
00:58:52,876 --> 00:58:56,010
Oh Hyun Nam deliberately joined Sales Team 3

899
00:58:56,776 --> 00:59:00,343
to get close to Director Yoo
and avenge her dad's death?

900
00:59:17,943 --> 00:59:22,176
Sometimes I wondered
if that day would ever come.

901
00:59:22,176 --> 00:59:24,676
That someone might find me.

902
00:59:25,676 --> 00:59:28,043
That someone might come looking for me.

903
00:59:28,043 --> 00:59:29,576
Who?

904
00:59:33,110 --> 00:59:35,410
I hope it doesn't happen.

905
01:00:42,710 --> 01:00:44,576
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?

906
01:00:45,876 --> 01:00:48,276
You ignored the photos,

907
01:00:48,276 --> 01:00:51,676
but the second I touched your husband,
you came running, huh?

908
01:00:51,676 --> 01:00:55,976
Where is he? I won't ask a third time.

909
01:01:01,210 --> 01:01:04,076
This is called Mist S.

910
01:01:05,876 --> 01:01:09,343
Drink 3 milliliters,
and in about five minutes you'll fall asleep.

911
01:01:09,343 --> 01:01:12,210
A sleep you'll never wake up from.

912
01:01:12,876 --> 01:01:15,610
I gave Kwon Tae Seong 6 milliliters.

913
01:01:19,410 --> 01:01:21,676
Have you lost your mind?

914
01:01:21,676 --> 01:01:23,543
Do you have any idea
how much that stuff costs?

915
01:01:23,543 --> 01:01:27,576
What's the price on your head?
Want in on this bill too?

916
01:01:32,510 --> 01:01:37,510
If he doesn't get the antidote
within the next hour, he'll die.

917
01:01:38,410 --> 01:01:42,143
You know exactly what that means, right?

918
01:01:46,876 --> 01:01:48,876
What do you want?

919
01:01:53,910 --> 01:01:55,843
Do you know who I am?

920
01:01:56,910 --> 01:01:58,410
I do.

921
01:01:59,776 --> 01:02:01,276
You do?

922
01:02:02,410 --> 01:02:05,310
I knew you'd figure it out.

923
01:02:07,143 --> 01:02:09,776
Or is that the work of that rude hacker?

924
01:02:11,843 --> 01:02:13,976
I know exactly who you are.

925
01:02:23,643 --> 01:02:26,043
Do you want to kill my husband?

926
01:02:36,276 --> 01:02:38,043
Then kill me too.

927
01:03:33,110 --> 01:03:34,543
Under no circumstances

928
01:03:34,543 --> 01:03:36,810
can we meet with anyone
other than the client.

929
01:03:36,810 --> 01:03:40,110
Because you messed with someone
you never should have.

930
01:03:40,110 --> 01:03:41,910
Things had been quiet for a while.

931
01:03:41,910 --> 01:03:43,410
- They said they saw Kingfisher?
- You're about to see

932
01:03:43,410 --> 01:03:45,143
another side of Kingfisher.

933
01:03:45,143 --> 01:03:47,310
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

934
01:03:47,310 --> 01:03:50,543
There's a strong possibility their base
of operations is somewhere nearby.

935
01:03:50,543 --> 01:03:52,743
These punks are crossing the line.

936
01:03:52,743 --> 01:03:55,110
It's 300 million won per head!

937
01:03:55,110 --> 01:03:56,776
I think we're really going to die.

938
01:03:56,776 --> 01:03:59,143
Why isn't Mommy answering?

939
01:03:59,976 --> 01:04:01,543
Mom and Dad...

940
01:04:01,543 --> 01:04:03,376
Director Yoo is awake.

941
01:04:03,376 --> 01:04:04,443
Never lose their dignity...

942
01:04:04,443 --> 01:04:06,976
Those darn flies won't stop buzzing.

943
01:04:06,976 --> 01:04:09,043
Maybe I should go deal with them.

